Multiply both sides by $ \sqrt{16 + h^2} $: $$
48 + 3h^2 = 20 \sqrt{16 + h^2}
$$

Since $ u > 0 $, $ u = \frac{20}{3} $, and so: $$
\sqrt{16 + h^2} = \frac{20}{3} \Rightarrow h^2 = \left( \frac{20}{3} \right)^2 - 16 = \frac{400}{9} - \frac{144}{9} = \frac{256}{9} \Rightarrow h = \frac{16}{3}
$$

Now, compute the distance between $ S = \left( \frac{16}{5}, \frac{12}{5} \right) $ and $ R = (1, \frac{16}{3}) $: $$
\Delta x = 1 - \frac{16}{5} = -\frac{11}{5}, \quad \Delta y = \frac{16}{3} - \frac{12}{5} = \frac{44}{15}
$$

$$
SR = \sqrt{ \left( -\frac{11}{5} \right)^2 + \left( \frac{44}{15} \right)^2 } = \sqrt{ \frac{121}{25} + \frac{1936}{225} }
$$

Convert to common denominator: $$
\frac{121}{25} = \frac{1089}{225}, \quad \text{so} \quad SR = \sqrt{ \frac{1089 + 1936}{225} } = \sqrt{ \frac{3025}{225} } = \frac{55}{15} = \frac{11}{3}
$$

$$
\boxed{\dfrac{11}{3}}
